cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LexiGround: Estimating Lexical Sensorimotor and Iconicity Ratings from Language Models"
message: "If you use LexiGround in your research, please cite this software."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Sathishkumar"
    given-names: "Shrisha"

repository-code: "https://github.com/shrishasat/lexiground"

url: "https://github.com/shrishasat/lexiground"

abstract: >
  LexiGround is an open-source Python package for retrieving and
  estimating lexical semantic ratings. The package provides access
  to human lexical norm ratings where available and uses pretrained
  SBERT embeddings with feature-specific Ridge regression models to
  estimate missing ratings for unseen words. Current models cover
  auditory, gustatory, haptic, interoceptive, olfactory, visual,
  motor-related, Minkowski sensorimotor, and iconicity dimensions.

keywords:
  - lexical semantics
  - sensorimotor norms
  - iconicity
  - word embeddings
  - SBERT
  - sentence transformers
  - Ridge regression
  - computational neuroscience
  - psycholinguistics


